{{Top}}
{{Expand|Behavior}}
{{Quote|If I ask? Then I think. And... as there are only two things that think... I must be one. Or the other.|The Scourge|<ref name="Dark Droids 1">[[Dark Droids 1|''Dark Droids'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:Motley_crowd-TFA.png|thumb|300px|A group of sentients from various species (and a droid), witness the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]] through [[sub-hyperspace]], from [[Takodana Castle]] on [[Takodana]]]]
'''Sentience''' (Sapience) was the quality of self-awareness, abstract thinking, and higher reasoning. Sentients possessed a personality, feeling emotionally as well as thinking intelligently.<ref name="Vandor">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]''</ref> Sentient [[species]] of [[the galaxy]] numbered in the tens of thousands, with [[3PO-series protocol droid]]s being programmed to recognize more than 30,000 of them.<ref name="M&A">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref> The number of individual people in the galaxy was numbered in the millions of billions. Some sentient species included [[human]]s,<ref name="Through the Turbulence">{{StoryCite|story=Through the Turbulence|book=Stories of Jedi and Sith}}</ref> [[Ewok]]s,<ref name="sweEWO">{{SWE|groups|ewoks|Ewoks}}</ref> [[Patitite]]s,<ref name="swePAT">{{SWE|groups|patitites|Patitites}}</ref> [[Gungan]]s,<ref name="sweGUN">{{SWE|locations|naboo|Naboo}}</ref> and [[Geonosian]]s.<ref name="sweGEO">{{SWE|locations|geonosis|Geonosis}}</ref>

'''Non-sentient''' organics of the animal kingdom were variously referred to as "creatures"<ref name="sweRAN">{{SWE|characters|rancor|rancor}}</ref><ref name="sweTAU">{{SWE|characters|tauntaun|tauntaun}}</ref> or "beasts."<ref name="sweRUP">{{SWE|characters|ruping|ruping}}</ref><ref name="sweNEX">{{SWE|characters|nexu|nexu}}</ref> There also existed creatures that appeared to have emerging sentience, such as the [[Zillo Beast]] and [[Purrgil]], being known as '''semi-sentient'''.<ref name="sweZIL">{{SWE|characters|zillobeast|Zillo Beast}}</ref><ref name="X-Wing #56">{{BuildXWingCite|56|Starfighter Aces}}</ref> The [[soul]] of the [[varactyl]] beast was considered simpler and purer than that of a sentient. Despite this, the creature was still intelligent in its own way.<ref name="M&A" /> [[Droid]]s were also capable of being sentient,<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref><ref name="Uncover">{{SW|url=news/marvel-star-wars-september-2023-preview|text=Uncover the ''Dark Droids'' Crossover Event in Marvel's September 2023 ''Star Wars'' Comics &ndash; Exclusive Preview}}</ref> although as with organic beings,<ref name="Return of the Jedi">{{Film|VI}}</ref> some droids, such as [[0-0-0]]<ref name="Aphra 40">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 40|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 40]]</ref> and [[EV-9D9]], took pleasure in inflicting pain upon others.<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

==Behavior==
{{Quote|Near-random bursts of free association, emotion-soaked ramblings, descents into holes of rumination and regret, decisions guided by delusions.|The [[Scourge]], describing organic sentient thought|<ref name="Dark Droids 1" />}}
The majority of sentient [[species]] dwelt on land, where frequent [[Water|rain]] sustains lush [[forest]]s, gardens, and [[grass]]y plains, although many species also inhabited dry ecosystems and rocky habitats. These species ability to adapt to survive on these harsher [[Planet|worlds]] made them better equipped to adapt offworld as well. Certain sentient species preferred to be immersed in liquids, and lived on worlds covered in water but could survive in airy environments without need for any [[Breath mask|breathing apparatus]] or [[Environment suit|environmental suits]].<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

==Sentient rights==
{{Quote|Sentients, please prepare for takeoff!|Pilot droid [[R-3X|RX-24]] addresses his passengers|<ref name="Droids in Distress">{{Rebels|Droids in Distress}}</ref>}}
Under the laws of the [[Galactic Republic]], sentient beings could not be used as [[Slavery|slaves]]. However, slavery thrived on certain remote planets, such as [[Tatooine]],<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> and was considered a profitable trade among the [[Zygerrian]]s.<ref name="sweZYG">{{SWE|groups|zygerrians|Zygerrians}}</ref> Droids were commonly treated as property and inferior to organic sentients,<ref name="Droids in Distress" /> and most droids were afforded programming that did not allow them to harm organic sentient beings, with notable exceptions such as [[police droid]]s<ref name="POL">{{SWE|technology|policedroid|police droid}}</ref> and [[battle droid]]s.<ref name="AOTC" /> Despite their programming, mechanical beings developed personality quirks and eventually sentience; however, this was suppressed through [[memory wipe]]s, a process opposed by those in support of [[droid rights]], who advocated for sentient rights for droids and raised the point of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Galactic Constitution]] declaring that all sentients were equal, and that slavery and forced servitude was outlawed.<ref name="Vandor" /> The [[Second Revelation]] was made up of sentient droids.<ref name="Uncover" />

==Sentience and the Force==
[[File:Jar_Jar_aotc.jpg|thumb|right|180px|Jar Jar Binks was a victim of being manipulated by Darth Sidious.]]
With his sentience, [[Darth Sidious]] manipulated unwitting [[senator]]s of the [[Galactic Senate]] such as [[Jar Jar Binks]] to grant him [[Galactic Emperor|supreme authority]],<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> although by the will of [[the Force]], Sidious was [[Battle of Endor|deposed]] by the [[Luke Skywalker|son]] of [[Anakin Skywalker|the Chosen One]],<ref name="CL2016" /> who was [[Reproduction|conceived]] by the [[midi-chlorian]]s&mdash;organisms that formed a symbiotic relationship with organic beings and communicated to them the Force's will;<ref name="TPM" /> the foundation of life and what connects and maintains the symbiotic relationship between the [[Living Force]]&mdash;the energy of all life&mdash;and the [[Cosmic Force]], which bound all things in [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Destiny">{{TCW|Destiny (The Clone Wars)}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], sentience encompasses<ref name="Vandor" /> both [[Wikipedia:Sentience|sentience]] and [[Wikipedia:Wisdom#Sapience|sapience]] in the real-world.<ref name="Sentience">{{WebCite|url=https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/sentience|text=Sentience|archivedate=20200806030809}}</ref><ref name="Sapience">{{WebCite|url=https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/sapience|text=Sapience|archivedate=20200610101424}}</ref>

